  "body": "**Blocked by:** none\n\n## Context\n\nReview follow-up from harvest issue #889. PR #469 (finding ed2125d67c), `backend/packages/data/src/chokePoint/relationOps.ts:77`: `loadCreatableRelationEdgeContext` declares its `input` parameter as `DeleteRelationInput`, but it performs the pre-flight checks of a create and is called by `createRelationWithClient` and `assertRelationCreatableWithClient`, both of which take `CreateRelationInput`. `DeleteRelationInput` is `Omit<CreateRelationInput, \"metadata\">`, so the code compiles today only because the narrower type happens to be assignable.\n\n## Task\n\nIn `relationOps.ts`, change the type of the `input` parameter of `loadCreatableRelationEdgeContext` from `DeleteRelationInput` to `CreateRelationInput`. Change nothing else.\n\n## Touches\n\n- backend/packages/data/src/chokePoint/relationOps.ts (the `input` parameter type of `loadCreatableRelationEdgeContext` only)\n\n## Scope\n\n### In scope\n\nThe one parameter type change.\n\n### Out of scope\n\nBehavior changes, the other functions in the file, and `DeleteRelationInput` itself.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- `loadCreatableRelationEdgeContext`'s `input` parameter is typed `CreateRelationInput`.\n- Both of its callers (`createRelationWithClient`, `assertRelationCreatableWithClient`) compile unchanged and `pnpm run verify` in `backend/` passes.\n\n\n<!-- crb-followup:v1 pr=469 key=ed2125d67c -->",
